On-device model
---------------
- omni_v0.1.onnx (wake word «Omni») — trained for this project with the
  openWakeWord v0.6.0 training stack (dscripka/openWakeWord, MIT) on
  synthetic speech from Piper voices (rhasspy/piper-voices; voices under
  individual CC BY licenses, training output MIT-compatible for this use).
  Metrics and provenance: training/OMNI_V0.1_REPORT.md. Vendored/adapted
  openwakeword train code (MIT): training/oww_train.py.
- openWakeWord models (melspectrogram.onnx, embedding_model.onnx,
  hey_jarvis_v0.1.onnx, v0.5.1) — dscripka/openWakeWord —
  (melspectrogram/embedding reused as acoustic frontend;
  hey_jarvis_v0.1 = legacy fallback phrase) —
  Apache License 2.0. Bundled under app/src/main/assets/wakeword/.
  SHA256 pins: see SHA256SUMS in the same directory.
- Gemma (on-device LLM used via MediaPipe, optional user-installed model) is
  governed by the Google Gemma Terms of Use and Gemma Prohibited Use Policy:
  https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
  The model weights are NOT distributed with this repository; the user
  supplies them and is responsible for complying with Gemma terms.

